  "notes": "Teen-pop carried by a soul/R&B vocal engine: 84–110 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and ballads down to 60, so the session window runs 60–110 with the mode on the 84 the research states for the debut single. The one drum fact that is a signature rather than a convention is the \"32nd-note bass-drum flutter under the groove\", and since the schema has no kick-subdivision field the flutter is encoded as the only thing that reaches the generator — a high kick `densityPerBar` of 4–8 with `syncopation` up at 0.48. The other two deltas are quoted directly: \"snare on 2&4 with a 16th ghost before 4\" is `ghost.pos` \"3a\" (on the e/&/a grid `engine/src/generators/grid.rs` parses, the 16th immediately *before* beat 4 is \"3a\"; \"4e\" falls after it), and \"hats mostly 16ths with an open hat on the last 8th\" is a pinned 16th base with the open hat on \"4&\". Harmony is the documented Fm–E♭–D♭ descending cell, i–VII–VI, with the extensions pushed towards sevenths because the vocal engine is R&B rather than Cheiron. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every probability in the drums block plus the two major 4-chord families: the entry says \"ballads in major with 4-chord loops\" without naming degrees, so I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V are this author's reading of that phrase and carry the lower weights. ⚠ `keys` is left inherited because the entry names one tonic.",
